WEBVTT

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.280
Go to the mainland?!

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.330
W--what?

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.270
Mr. Porte!

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.130
Bell, go with her.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.210
Howard and I will wait for Kaoru and such.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.290
Okay.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.640
I wonder if old man Porte will be okay.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.410
Mr. Porte!

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.120
Menori!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.010
Howard!

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.230
Are you okay?

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.290
Just what exactly happened?

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:55.340
Just when we'd taken off, we got in a fight with 'em.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:58.790
And to save us, Mr. Porte...

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.690
It's too early to be sure. Mr. Porte will probably be fine.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.580
We saw him falling with a parachute.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:06.890
Really?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.480
Luna and Bell are searching for him right now.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.810
We should go too!

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.860
--Mr. Porte!
--Mr. Porte!

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:28.640
Mr. Porte!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.460
He should be around here...

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.760
Over there!

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:49.870
Mr. Porte!

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.370
We'd better help him quick!

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:59.390
Well, I'm really glad you're okay.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:05.060
But you're lucky this is all you got away with after falling from such a height!

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:08.020
It's because I'm made of tougher stuff than the lot of you!

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.740
You mustn't move.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.190
Looks like you'd better take it easy for a while.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.470
I guess so.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:23.280
Just when we thought we could escape from this planet, the transport ship is destroyed.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.870
Don't worry! We've still got Adam's ruins, don't we?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.120
If only we did...

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.720
Don't tell me... the ruins...

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.710
Okay, let's go to the ruins.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.730
It <i>is</i> in the direction of the ruins.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.080
No way...

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.310
What do we do if the ruins are destroyed?

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.480
Could you stand something like that happening?

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.780
It's the river! We'd better detour!

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.070
We don't have time for that!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.680
Gravity's lighter around here, so we'll just jump over the river like it was nothing!

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:23.770
Just watch!

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:24.970
Hey, Howard!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.840
I stopped? This is odd! If I just run, it'll work out somehow! No, it's no use!

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:35.430
Howard!

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:43.790
It's weird... Usually I could jump so easily.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.390
Almost like the gravity control unit stopped.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.490
Looks like somethin' happened to the ruins after all!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.480
Anyways, let's hurry!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.360
It's hopeless.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:38.660
Dad...

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.510
Mom!

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:42.180
Adam!

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.320
You can't do that, Adam! It's dangerous!

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.280
But my mom and dad...

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.340
Won't be able to use this for anythin'.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:18.630
It's hopeless...

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.120
Work, damn it! Work! Work!

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:23.770
It's pointless.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.940
We don't know that for sure!

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.190
If we get this working, we can manage something!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:29.660
Shingo...

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.720
Work! Work!

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:34.080
Shingo, he told'ja to stop!

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.890
No use'll come outta doin' that!

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:41.090
The gravity control unit's screwed up and the reactor's beaten to bits!

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.770
Whatever you do, this thing's finished! It won't work!

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.110
Hey, hey! Don't give up on it so easily!

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.880
If this doesn't work, we can't get home!

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.680
Of course we know that!

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:53.620
In that case...

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.240
If there was something we could do, I'd be doing it.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.890
Even you, gramps...

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:02.540
Hey, why don't you give it another good look? Maybe you'll find something you can do.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.280
No way...

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:23.690
Adam...

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.510
Luna!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:31.160
What should I do? There's nothing left here for me!

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:35.240
Because of this, I don't know how I'll be able to find where my mom and dad are!

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:36.480
Adam...

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:43.570
Don't give up hope just yet. There's still the main computer on the mainland.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:47.960
It might give us clues about your mother and father.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:49.830
Mainland?

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.970
That's right, the mainland!

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:56.810
Go to the mainland?

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:02.880
Yes, don't you all remember? There was a hologram of this planet in the ruins.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:09.180
There was a main computer on the mainland that was controlling the terraforming machine here.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:13.830
And these ruins might have been launched from the mainland, right?

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:18.630
So if we go to the mainland, there might be another space ship!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:19.870
Yes.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.370
I'm against it.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.210
I mean, think about it.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.730
We don't know if there'll be a space ship on the mainland or not.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:30.560
There might not even be food, let alone a space ship.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:34.830
Instead of doing something pointless, we should just wait here for a rescue ship.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:38.360
But we don't know when a rescue ship will come.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.270
W--- well that's true...

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:47.020
Everyone wants to go home to the colony, right? Then let's take a chance on the mainland!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.270
But how do you plan on getting as far as the mainland?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.070
Maybe we can make a ship.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:01.340
Ship?

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:06.110
Yes. There still seem to be plenty of parts in the ruins we can use.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.160
We can put it together out of those parts. What do you think, Nr. Porte?

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.630
It'll be tricky.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.590
Ships that float on the water are outside my area of expertise.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:21.480
From what I saw, there weren't any parts that could generate the power you'd need to cross the sea.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.330
That's why we should all start searching now...

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.810
"Search," you say...

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:34.230
I understand how you feel, Luna, but it'd be impossible to get power out of any of those parts.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:35.660
Chako...

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:39.070
There's no need to rush to a decision.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.470
And there's the matter of Mr. Porte's health.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:46.640
For the time being, let's rebuild the basis of our lifestyle, and decide what to do afterwards.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.870
Very well.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.230
A week passed since then.

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.430
And our life in Everyone's House had begun again.

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:33.410
But everyone was in low spirits.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:37.980
The shock was as great as our hopes had been.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.880
Howard, I'm going to look for food!

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:52.940
Howard!

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:00.590
Won't someone get here soon?

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.370
Howard!

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:09.780
Fine, forget about it! I'll go on my own!

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:10.980
Luna.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.910
I'll go with you.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.610
Thanks, Sharla.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.660
What? A container from the transport ship?

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:26.810
I found it while I was searching for food.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.960
I think it probably fell out during the explosion.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:34.640
And when I looked inside, there was something that looked like a gravity control unit.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.110
Really?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.040
Yes.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.060
I wanted to ask Shingo about it, but in that state...

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.380
Great! Let's check it out!

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.620
Luna, this way!

00:13:58.870 --> 00:13:59.690
Over there!

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:23.320
But to think you came somewhere like this on your own.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.540
Well everyone's been in such sour moods lately.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.940
I felt like I couldn't let things go on like this any longer.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:29.990
This way.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.420
Sharla...

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.670
In here.

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:35.240
Take a look.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:43.490
It certainly looks like a gravity control unit.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:50.990
What are you doing?

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:53.060
Seeing whether or not it works.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:58.120
It's not like we'd be telling them that much later.

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:00.820
And I wouldn't want to get their hopes up for no reason.

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:36.590
Luna!

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.210
I'm scared!

00:15:38.510 --> 00:15:40.340
Hold on! I'll shut it down!

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:49.570
Luna!

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:50.960
What's wrong?

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:53.620
Adam!

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:57.560
What's wrong?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:01.460
I don't know. Maybe something happened to Luna.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.370
Alright, we'd better go too.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:05.880
Howard!

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:08.840
What is it?

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:11.210
It's an emergency! Let's go!

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.090
An emergency?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.270
I guess it certainly worked.

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:24.670
Luna?

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.290
Luna, where are you?

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:31.420
Luna!

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:33.780
Snap out of it!

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:35.390
Luna!

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:37.120
Sharla!

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.390
Are you okay?

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:42.290
We're in here! Hurry up! Luna... Luna...

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:48.260
Luna, snap out of it.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:49.790
Ouch...

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:50.880
Huh?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:54.330
Everyone!

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:56.090
What happened?

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.310
We already heard from Sharla.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:00.410
Yeesh, what nonsense have you been up to?

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.920
Without even knowing how to use it!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.520
Sorry for making you all worry.

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:09.710
There's no need for Luna to apologize.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.430
Luna did it for all of you!

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:16.120
For us?

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:20.320
Don't you realize the way you've been acting?

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.540
Staring into space from dawn until dusk, as if you were dead!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:24.710
What did you say?

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.390
It's just like Sharla says.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.010
I think so too.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:34.610
Maybe you didn't know, but Luna's been searching for parts for the ship every night!

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.710
And yet, you all...

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.590
Sharla, you knew?

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.140
That's how it was.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.410
Everyone, it seems to be okay!

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.880
Yep, nothin's broken at all!

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:48.930
Really?

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:50.320
Set the area...

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.610
...adjust the output...

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:54.260
...and switch on!

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:14.060
With this, we might just be able to make a ship to reach the mainland!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.340
Let me do it too!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:26.810
Shall we go check it out?

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:29.770
To the mainland.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.990
We certainly can't stay the way we are, after all.

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:34.680
Menori...

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:43.940
What?

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.570
There was a gravity control unit?

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.280
There was one in a container that fell out of the transport ship.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:52.230
It's just one for use in a power shovel, though.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.810
But is it okay?

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:58.270
Even if you go to the mainland, there's no guarantee there'll be a space ship.

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.790
We've decided to take a chance on the mainland.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:05.810
It'd just be boring to wait around here like this, after all.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.370
Looks like you've all decided.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.970
Very well. I'll draw up the bluepr--ouch...

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:14.470
I'll make them!

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.660
Let me make them, Mr. Porte.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:19.270
Can you do it?

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:20.920
I'll try my best.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:22.870
It won't be easy.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.610
I'll help out too.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.470
Then let's let Shingo and Chako take care of it.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.080
The mainland...

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.610
It'd be nice if your mother and father were there, Adam.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:55.190
If we meet them, there are things I'd like to ask them.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.520
Things you'd like to ask?

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:58.570
Yes.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:04.270
The first time I heard that mysterious voice was when I was attacked by the giant lizard.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:11.430
And also when we were attacked by the giant animals.

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:20.090
We were always saved by that voice.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:24.300
!pmuJ

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:28.190
And we had been doing so well for so long...

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:34.490
But I don't know why I can hear it and nobody else can.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.540
And Adam, with you as well.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.770
Why can only you and I communicate?

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.060
I have a feeling your parents would tell me.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:10.190
Yeesh! Give it a rest with the 'hmmmmm'!

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:12.590
Tell us straight out whether we can do it or not!

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:15.260
There's nothing I can say.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.240
What's up with that?

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:19.120
What's wrong with it?

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.520
Nobody said anything was wrong with it.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.630
And forget wrong, it's very well done.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:25.870
In that case...

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:32.770
The problem is whether we can get the parts for it just from the ruins and the transport ship.

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:36.330
But if we can find the parts, we can make the ship, right?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.280
Perhaps.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:41.990
Don't worry about it! Even I can find parts!

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:44.960
That's right! If we all search, we're sure to find the parts!

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:48.630
Right. Then should we start looking for parts right away?

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:50.810
Yeah!

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:01.910
Menori, what about the one in there?

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:06.560
This one?

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.070
No, the one in there!

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.010
In there?

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:15.890
This one?

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:18.410
No, the one on the left!

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:21.630
If you're going to talk that way,
why don't you do it yourself?

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:23.210
Okay, I'm sorry.

00:22:30.520 --> 00:22:31.310
Chako!

00:22:43.610 --> 00:22:44.920
Watch your step!

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:46.830
I'm okay.

00:23:03.740 --> 00:23:06.370
Well, the ship-building has finally begun!

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:13.340
But if we can't find enough parts, Mr. Porte won't give the vital blueprints the okay.

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:15.220
Keep at it, Shingo!

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:17.990
Nothin' to worry about, Luna.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.560
The bond between those two is super-duper strong.

00:23:21.890 --> 00:23:24.290
There's affection behind his strictness.

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:29.690
Next time: But we don't even have enough materials
